le-title>Fast and accurate phylogeny reconstruction algorithms based on the minimum-evolution principle.</article-title><source>J Comput Biol</source><year>2002</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>687</fpage><lpage>705</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12487758</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1089/106652702761034136</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gu&#x000e9;noche</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Garreta</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Gascuel O, Sagot M-F</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Can we have confidence in a tree representation?</article-title><source>Proceedings of the First International Conference on Biology, Informatics, and Mathematics: 3-5 May 2000; Montpellier</source><year>2000</year><publisher-name>Berlin: Springer-Verlag</publisher-name><fpage>45</fpage><lpage>56</lpage><comment>[Hofmann A (series editor): <italic>Lecture Notes in Computer Science</italic>, vol 2066.]</comment></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>